<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχυτρ-ίστρια</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>woman who</i>
			
			<i>gathered the bones</i> from a funeral pile <i>into an
			urn</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Min.</u>
				315c
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχυτίστρια</span>
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				313.41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>woman who exposed children</i>, acc. to Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				289
			</span></i> (but cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγχύτριαι</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
